!! What it does

A zettelkasten-style note app for TiddlyWiki. Notes live under the `knowledge/…` title namespace and link via short refs (`[[Foo]]`) thanks to the [[namespace|$:/plugins/rimir/namespace]] plugin. The app surfaces those notes through a mindmap-driven navigation surface with a built-in preview pane.

!! Features

* Mindmap navigation — full-width forest of all areas (each area is a top-level branch). Area roots are expanded by default, their descendants collapsed; user expansions persist across reloads. Powered by `rimir/mindmap`'s `knowledge-tree` producer.
* Selecting a node opens the mindmap's built-in preview pane on the right with the note body, a `kn.type` pill chooser at the top (15 types grouped core / entity / structural), and backlinks / outgoing references at the bottom (namespace-aware via `ns-backlinks` / `ns-forwardlinks`).
* Tier × type filter chips above the mindmap — multi-select; chip clicks prune the tree with ancestor preservation so paths to matching descendants stay visible.
* Quick-capture from the topbar — title + body modal. Lands at `knowledge/<area>/<slug>` where `<area>` is the currently-selected area pill (falls back to `knowledge/inbox/<slug>` when no area is active). Autocomplete suggests existing matches; duplicate titles disable Create.
* Type-specific capture forms — each note type can ship `forms/capture-<type>` with extra modal fields. First example: ''source'' (TZK-style) with caption / author / medium / url / published / consume-status / consume-date.
* Three note tiers — `fleeting`, `developing`, `evergreen` — stamped on the `kn.tier` field. The tier filter chips read this; promotion UX is currently captured via the popup-edit modal or direct field edit (dedicated tier-pill UI was retired in 0.1.20).
* Backlinks panel reads namespace's reverse index (`ns-backlinks`) so context-resolved references are counted.
* Starter mount `kn` so any tiddler can write `[[kn/topics/foo]]` and reach knowledge content.
* Custom pseudo `_index` — inside an absolute ref, `…/_index` resolves to the topic's `index` or `README`.

!! Prerequisites

* [[appify|$:/plugins/rimir/appify]]
* [[mindmap|$:/plugins/rimir/mindmap]] (≥ 0.2.29; a mindmap engine like `rimir/mindmap-elixir` is needed for the canvas to render)
* [[namespace|$:/plugins/rimir/namespace]]
* [[theme|$:/plugins/rimir/theme]]

!! Quick start

# Open the FAB → "Knowledge".
# Click an area pill in the topbar (or ''+ Area'' to create one).
# Topbar → ''+ Note''. Type a title and (optionally) some body wikitext.
# Click a node in the mindmap to preview it. Click again on a different node to switch.
# Type `[[Foo]]` in a note body to link a (possibly future) note.

